No third-party source code may be added to this repository unless its
licence is compatible with the posture above and it is recorded in
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md. In particular, Apache-2.0 code (for example from
MeshCentral) requires preserving its licence text and NOTICE, and marking
modified files — see docs/adr/INTEGRATION-OWNERSHIP.md.

Run `scripts/check_licenses.py` before any distribution. It fails on
copyleft dependencies and, with --strict, on licences with use
restrictions. Two dependencies (react-leaflet, @react-leaflet/core) are
currently under the Hippocratic Licence 2.1, which is not OSI-approved and
restricts *use*; that is an open product decision, not a settled fact.
